<section>
    <h2>Two options… neither is great</h2>
    <table class="compare">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th></th>
                <th>Real HTTP calls</th>
                <th>Handwritten mocks</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Realism</td>
                <td class="good">Real responses</td>
                <td class="bad">What we imagine the API returns</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Speed</td>
                <td class="bad">Slow (network)</td>
                <td class="good">Instant</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Stability in CI</td>
                <td class="bad">Depends on the provider (quotas, outages)</td>
                <td class="good">Stable</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Cost</td>
                <td class="bad">Paying APIs bill every call (OpenAI, payments…)</td>
                <td class="good">Free</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Secrets</td>
                <td class="bad">API keys in CI</td>
                <td class="good">None</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Maintenance</td>
                <td class="meh">None… as long as the API answers</td>
                <td class="bad">Tedious, and it drifts</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>Today, we usually have two options: real HTTP calls, or handwritten mocks. Let's compare.</p>
        <p>[click] Realism. Real calls give real responses. Mocks give what we imagine the API returns.</p>
        <p>[click] Speed. Real calls are slow: they use the network. Mocks are instant.</p>
        <p>[click] Stability. Real calls depend on the provider: quotas, outages. Mocks are stable.</p>
        <p>[click] Cost. Paying APIs bill every call, so every test run costs money. Mocks are free.</p>
        <p>[click] Secrets. Real calls need API keys in the CI. Mocks need nothing.</p>
        <p>[click] Maintenance. Real calls: nothing to do, as long as the API answers. Mocks: a lot of work. And they drift away from the real API.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
